Package: sparseDist
Title: Fast Distances, Nearest Neighbours and Graphs for Sparse Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Gennaro",
           family = "Gambardella",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "gambalab.bioinformatics@gmail.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7517-1347"))
Description: Computes column-wise distances and similarities, memory-bounded
    k-nearest-neighbour searches, and shared-nearest-neighbour graphs for
    large, highly sparse data. Jaccard, cosine, Euclidean, Manhattan,
    Jensen-Shannon, Pearson correlation and covariance are supported, either
    among the columns of a single matrix or between the columns of two
    matrices. A full matrix needs memory quadratic in the number of columns, so
    a blocked search is also provided that returns only the k nearest
    neighbours of each column and never materialises the whole result; those
    neighbourhoods can then be reweighted by overlap into a sparse graph ready
    for community detection. The kernels are written in C++ using
    'RcppArmadillo', are parallelised with 'OpenMP' where the compiler supports
    it, and report progress through 'RcppProgress'. The Jaccard, cosine,
    Euclidean and Manhattan sparse kernels traverse only stored non-zero
    entries, so their pairwise cost depends on sparsity rather than on the full
    matrix dimensions.
